\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces MSP-CNN direct RT regression baseline architecture. A lightweight 1-D temporal ConvNet maps an EEG trial window to a scalar reaction-time prediction. A learned $1\times 1$ channel-squeeze layer (128$\rightarrow $48) is followed by residual depthwise-separable stages with anti-aliased temporal downsampling, segment-wise pooling (2 and 4 segments; mean+max), and an MLP head.}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ch1_regression}{{2}{10}{MSP-CNN direct RT regression baseline architecture. A lightweight 1-D temporal ConvNet maps an EEG trial window to a scalar reaction-time prediction. A learned $1\times 1$ channel-squeeze layer (128$\rightarrow $48) is followed by residual depthwise-separable stages with anti-aliased temporal downsampling, segment-wise pooling (2 and 4 segments; mean+max), and an MLP head}{figure.2}{}}
